f=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T14:11:19-08:00","id":341207,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm feeling somewhat jealous of your free time, given IRL is actively trying to prevent me from writing and I have to keep it in head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:51:08-08:00","id":341606,"title":"","content":"Free time? nope, not the case for me- I'm just forcing myself to take some breaks and do something I like in my life :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:56:44-08:00","id":341779,"title":"","content":"Well, I cannot afford taking breaks now, it's enough troubling for my schedules I spare time for foruming. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T12:02:37-08:00","id":344992,"title":"","content":"So, one of the things I've thought about was the Heiromagus of the Guardians. Eventually, I came to the conclusion that that the mythical messiah of magic must be a symbol- another objective that Magic itself is trying to accomplish. Once the symbol of Atlantis was destroyed, Magic made a symbol of hope- a path through which the symbol might be restored. But just as there were many failed &quot;Atlantean Empires&quot;, there were also many false Heiromagi. Once Magic would successfully be able to manifest that symbol in someone, it would be the first milestone in restoring itself to its original curse. Until then, it would just have to try again and again.<br /> <br /> And finally- the Underworld!<br /> <br /> In order to understand the Underworld, one must understand Death. I don't just speak about the phenomena, but about the entity- the ancient Lemurian who cursed all humanity. The truth is that the Underworld has predated death- it was an old realm, older than even the Lemurians, the Exrachs, Gaea or any other entity (with the exception of God.. perhaps). It was the eternal &quot;waiting room&quot;- or more exactly, a recycle bin. Nothing was meant to &quot;die&quot;- only to go there, wait some time and return all new and shiny. During that time, Inferno's flames still didn't burned at the bottom of the Great Below, and the Supernal was way outside of man's reach. There was no Hell nor Heaven for the mortal souls- only endless cycles of death and rebirth, and it worked perfectly.<br /> <br /> The first ones to fuck it up were the Exrachs.<br /> <br /> When they summoned the Abyss, broke Atlantis and conquered the Supernal, many of the Old Gods have died. Some died fighting. Others were executed for symbolizing things the Exrachs didn't liked. While many of those symbols has fallen to the Abyss, with it being the only power able to destroy symbols, the Kings of the Lie didn't had the time to properly dispose of all of the Old Gods- and so, they threw them the furthest they could- into the pits of the Underworld. Those broken symbols became what most people know as the Chthonians- dead things which never lived. Those creatures has ventured deeper and deeper, searching for a sanctuary from the wrath of the &quot;New Gods&quot;- until they eventually found some warmth for they cold bones. The Exrachs brought the Abyss to the world. The Old Gods found Inferno.<br /> <br /> While the opening to the Lower Depths was the first step for changing the nature of the Underworld, it wasn't the last.While infernal beings mad managed to enter the world and steal souls, most of the souls kept going up and down, maintaining the cycle. That is, until Lemuria has fallen by the hands of mankind, and then used their powerful magic to change reality itself. While each of the Lemurains has done quite a damage, Death did the most- he was a powerful necromancer, and his curse was to lock the Gates of Death- but only from one side. Souls could get in, but not to get out. That curse was the way death was defined, and the words were written on a tablet which was hidden in the depth of the Underworld. To protect it, a great guardian was created- a monstrous three headed hound named Kerebros, or as it is more modernly known, Cerberus. Those were the first Old Laws to be written, and that was the first Dead Dominion to be formed.<br /> <br /> Eventually, the curse had event greater effect then Death himself imagined- for by disrupting the cycle of souls, some souls had managed to linger behind, withholding their fall to the Below. Those were the first ghosts to take form- but still, they didn't formed in the Twilight. They were too distant to effect the world, and could only manifest as weak visages and echos. In an addition, the curse of Death pulled them like gravity, forcing them to leave the world no more than a year and a day since their death. Through time, many other things had fallen to the Underworld- forgotten concepts, shattered dreams, fallen stories. While nations were lost in the depths, and the once dry underworld has started to flow with rivers, made from the tears of the dead. While the Chthonians devoured those who wondered too deep and the demons of Inferno stole those who weren't careful enough, some of the oldest souls had managed to find the old tablet, pass its guardian and redefine death according to their own view, establishing their own Dominions and Laws. Those were the first Deathlords in the world, and with each Deathlord who rose another river has started to flow. Some of the dead, however, were too old but not powerful enough, and instead were crushed into themselves, creating mini black holes of death. Eventually, those black holes were united and fell to the depths of existence, even below the Lower Depths, creating a place were even time and space died and which erased every memory of what that was consumed by it- Oblivion.<br /> <br /> While the underworld has turned from a waiting room into an half a museum- half junkyard, the Fallen World managed to maintain itself quite good. While most of the empires and nations which existed during that time had feared the dead, one has ruled them- it was one of the city states which ruled the land who would become Sumer. That land was different than the other city states around it. It wasn't ruled by a man, but by a woman. Its leader didn't belonged to one of the Wolf Tribes, but a powerful magician who was respected by the wolf people as having the &quot;soul of a beast&quot;. Finally, that land didn't talked the language of the spirits, and instead worked to rule the Dead. That land was Kigal, and its lady was Ereshkigal.<br /> <br /> And that was the finale stage at shaping the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Ereshkigal ruled the Gates of Death by the use of a powerful artifact called the Throne of Mists. The throne, made out of the bones of a Chthonian killed by Lady herself, has allowed her to force the Avernian Gates open and let her force the dead to her will. There was one condition- that only the ruler of the living may rule the dead. That meant that only the recognized leader of the city state may use the artifact, else Irkalla's gates would be opened uncontrollably. While for many years Ereshkigal ruled undisturbed, it has all changed once her sister- a sorceress named Inanna, came to a visit. Unlike Ereshkigal, who was cold and brutal, Inanna was whimsy and unexpected. Ereshkigal, knowing that her sister wasn't to be trusted, had to let her enter her city because of the old family traditions, but she had her to leave all of her magic tools behind. As it was expected, the two fought when they met in the palace- until Inanna, who knew nothing about the power of the Throne, had decided to show her displeasure and sit on the chair.<br /> <br /> And then all Hell broke loose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T13:15:03-08:00","id":345063,"title":"","content":"Once she sat on the artifact, all of the Avernian Gates in Kigal and around it were opened, allowing hundreds of ghosts to swarm the land. Ereshkigal had to use all of her power to maintain her rule, and with her anger has sent her foolish sister to be executed by hanging. While her sister begged for a second chance- Ereshkigal refused, not even coming to her sister's execution. While that was supposed to be the end, it was only the beginning- for just has Inanna was between life and death, a powerful being which escaped thanks to her efforts offered its help- it had two faces, and named itself as both Gala-tur and Kur-jara. The being, who was more then a ghost yet less then a Deathlord, offered the dying sorceress a second chance- and she agreed. She didn't knew (although most chances that even if she did it wouldn't have changed anything about her actions), but one of the Deathlords who changed death had added a loophole- that once one of the dead would be one with the living, the year and a day time limit would be terminated. By agreeing to share a body with the creature, Inanna became the first of the Bound, the being became the first geist- and so, the Law was broken.<br /> <br /> And with it, Kigal has fallen.<br /> <br /> The Gates were opened once again- but this time, they didn't closed. The surprised and weak Ereshkigal, who still didn't replenished her power after the previous incident couldn't do much- she was only able to stabilize her kingdom as her sister escaped and the angry dead had made the realm which ruled them for so many years to sink to the bottom of the Underworld. Thanks to the loophole, now the dead could walk side by side with the living, hidden from all while existing in the Deathly Frequency of the Twilight. Now, Geists could offer second chances to the dying, giving them the Keys for the Gates of the Underworld. And those people, those Sin Eaters, could take the pieces the reality through away and recreate the world in the way they liked it- the realm of broken symbols was them to rule, giving the Bound accesses to unlimited potential.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in the depths of the Underworld, Ereshkligal survived. Filled with anger, she cursed her sister and used her magic to subdue Kerebros. She redefined Death again, this time making it into cold and merciless as her. She became a deathlord, and helped the survivors to find their way out of the Below using her knowledge in the secret ways of the Underworld. Those people still exist, and still serve her in the form of an old, almost dead conspiracy of hunters and exorcists.<br /> <br /> It was also during that time that the beings named as the Five Horseman rose in the underworld. Those powerful ghosts have achieved a state equal, if not greater, then the Deathlords themselves. Unlike the Deathlords, they weren't bound to their Dominion, but rose above it, gathering armies of the dead under their flag and riding through the dark caves in a war of conquest. They became the manifestation of Death itself. Unbound by Laws or definition, they were originally only four- for once, Death always had a reason. With the rise with the belief in chance and misfortune, the number of deaths which weren't under the dominions of the 4 Horseman grew, allowing one of the Deathlords to ascend as the Grey Horseman.<br /> <br /> While most of the times the societies of the Bound were under a low profile, from time to time they managed to rose to greatness. One of those times was in Egypt- when two rival krewes used the people's faith in the Iremite mythologies to gain power and connect themselves to an underworld no one of them ever visited. Eventually, the two krewes had merged together, and from the combinations of Duat's old spells and the Underworld's chaotic energies many great and terrible creations were made. Through the existence of old Egypt the krewes and the Arisen had both worked together and against each other in a weird alliance.<br /> <br /> So, let's talk about the Underworld itself- as it was said before, it is both a junkyard and a museum. All pieces of human histories are thrown into there, and the Authochtonous Depths are even more of a junkyard than the rest of the realm. It isn't a reflection, but literal pieces of time which are no longer actual to, well, anything. The more relevant something is, the less strongly it shows up in the Depths. This is where your lost socks and keys go to- a place which mixes up everything to create both wonders and horrors never imagined by man. While the rivers may be described as the &quot;tears of the dead&quot;, they are more exactly made out of souls- or what is left of those who don't manage to move on after thousands of years in the Great Below. The Ferryman are the manifestations of those thousands of souls, which never give anything for free. The Kereboi are also manifestations- but not of souls. Instead, they are the manifestations of the Old Laws themselves. The complicated mythologies of the Bound are created by using the right &quot;junk&quot; and piecing everything together. Abmortals are made by the same loopholes which created the Sin Eaters- making the Bound into a specific, extremely powerful and accepted type of Abmortals.<br /> <br /> Finally, all rivers flow to the Ocean of Fragments. Its waters are made from endless souls, and at its bottom is found the first tablet of Death. Its water swirl around the Oblivion, which grants it is &quot;erasing&quot; abilities. Everything the Ocean takes flows right to the black hole, where it is destroyed for all eternity. However, below the fourth Depth is not Oblivion- it lies even under it, below the Lower Depths themselves, creating a huge waterspout which penetrates even the flames of Inferno. The blackness is actually the door the the realm of the original Death- and those who dare to go there meet face to face with the Kerebros. Once a person goes even deeper, he'll reach the burning flames of Inferno, creating what most people think about when they hear about &quot;Hell&quot;. Also, Psychopomps are the original denizens of the Underworld, who still try to guide the souls outside of the Below.<br /> <br /> next, I'll talk about Demon and the post Lemurian God Machine!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-19-2014, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:15:21-08:00","id":345686,"title":"","content":"So. I've thought about it, and I've noticed that unlike the other realms in my cosmology, the Underworld is kinda,, quite. There are no cosmological maneuvers or godly manipulations in that realm, and I'm not sure if I like it. The closest I have is that the five Horseman gather the armies of the dead in order to become more influential in the Underworld (that is, each tries to become the leading cause of death). I'm not sure that I like it that way- I mean, what I like is complicated cosmologies for no reason and great factions which manipulate reality. So, here are few changes- or more exactly, re-interpretations- of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> First, you have the Chthonians. Those dead Gods are barely united, with each being a power by its own. Some demand worship from poor souls. Others just devour them. While few may seek for a way to &quot;fix&quot; themselves, most don't care about it. They have lost their war, and now they are just broken, shells of their former self. They have invited the Lower Depths to the world out of spite, and they still have an alliance with the forces of Inferno and other &quot;close&quot; Lower Depths. Some of the more motivated dead gods seek to break the Supernal itself, turning the whole world into an Underworld. The most, however, just don't care.<br /> <br /> The second faction is the Deathlords, all united under the banner of the Five Horsemen. One of the more colorful groups in the celestial game, each Deathlord had re-defined death by its &quot;ascension&quot;. They all have started as human souls, who slowly became something more then they once were- into geists, the archetypes of their own death. By collecting the pieces they find relevant in the Underworld, They expand their own dominion and understanding of what Death is, until they come to the Ocean of Fragments. There, they finally leave behind any semblance who who they once were, becoming the lies they told themselves they were. Those who manage to pass through the fourth Depth and pass the original Kerebros can change the Laws of Death to become Deathlords.<br /> <br /> The Kereboi are the third faction. While those creatures are the manifestation of the Old Laws which were written by the local Deathlord, they actually aren't bound to their will. They are the creations of the curse of Death, and the byproducts of the Deathlord's ascension. The Deathlords are, after all, beings of chaos and change, who mutate the Great Below to fit to their own view. The Kereboi, however, force the Laws which were made by them- even if it is against the will of their &quot;master&quot;. making it that even the Deathlord can't break its own Law. It may change them, of course, or remove them entirely- by as long as they are valid, the Kereboi makes sure that everything would work as written. That is why the Horsemen are seen which such a respect- they have freed themselves from their own Laws, becoming a force free forever from the curse of Death.<br /> <br /> The fourth group is the Ferrymen. The manifestation of countless of souls in the form of the rivers, they lead the dead toward the Ocean for they'll all lose their &quot;self&quot; in a form of transcendence. You may call them the &quot;agents of Oblivion&quot;, but they prefer to use the Greek name, Lethe. They don't seek to end the world, but to lose their identity and become one- a collective potential of all of mankind. The waters of the Ocean are the most refined form of human soul, and in that form the souls could be &quot;recycled&quot; and used again to bring new life to the world. Leviathan is the manifestation of that collective- not a Kerebros, but the manifestation of humanity's most refined &quot;truth&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finally, the psychopomps. Those beast like creatures are, as it was said, the original dwellers of the Underworld. They led human souls back to the surface, and made sure that no one would loose his way. Yet, once Death closed the gate, they have lost their purpose- but they don't give up. They found other paths, ones that even Death didn't knew about. Some led to a place so bright that it could burn the weakest of souls- the Empyrean. Others led to an ever burning fire which tormented the wicked- Inferno. By leading the souls to the &quot;Heaven&quot; or &quot;Hell&quot;, they have found a new purpose- and so, some of them decided to make themselves into those who judge mankind. Others still seek after a way to open the Gates, and few even managed to allow reincarnation for certain souls. The greatest among the Psychopomps are called the Orphean Lords- those who know the paths of the Great Below, and may even return to the world of the living. They are the rivals of the Ferrymen, for each of them have a different view of what should happen to the human soul.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:38:18-08:00","id":346121,"title":"","content":"So, let's talk Demon.<br /> <br /> After the fall of Lemuria, the God Machine was left alone. Without anyone to monitor it, it was left with its finale mission- what rise must fall. What's fallen may rise again. Those were the last commands given to it by its makers, which meant to maintain the status que until, one day, they would return to their rightful place. Yet, all but 9 Lemurians (I changed it from 8 to 9, sue me) were killed when mankind rebelled, and there was no hope for them to reclaim their place as the leading empire of the world. Instead, new empires rose to power- only to fall, again and again. Yet, the God Machine doesn't know that its last mission is meaningless- it only known it must follow it, working to preserve the existing state, so the world won't become worse (or better) then it originally was.<br /> <br /> With mankind being the most common intelligent being, the God Machine knew it had to supervise it- and in order to do so, it had to grow in strength, feeding from the energies of the Empyrean in the material world, up to the point that eventually even its makers had to ask for permission from it before acting (such as in the case of Strife). In order to better accomplish its job, it has started to create artificial intelligences to guide and manipulate mankind toward their wanted &quot;destiny&quot;. The first creation were horrible failures- man-animal hybrids which no man dared to stand against. Still, the God Machine was patient- until eventually it managed to create the first &quot;angels&quot; to serve it, and the greatest among them was no other then Lucifer.<br /> <br /> At first, the angels worked efficiently, and the God Machine had felt it achieved its goal. However, it didn't understood that it made the angels a bit too well- for the Covers he created for them had also contained the traces of free will and open mind which all of humanity had shared. And so, one day, Lucifer has looked upon the world and thought why did he, one of the greatest beings in the world, had served the God Machine? What the plan of its maker even was? Why he, who could make his own destiny, had to listen to the commands of a mindless husk?..<br /> <br /> Then, he understood that he could act against the Machine. And by doing so, he Fell- and fell hard.<br /> <br /> The God Machine immediately recognized the danger, and sent legions of angels to capture his wayward &quot;child&quot;. But Lucifer was powerful, and he fought. Still, eventually he failed, and was captured by the God Machine- who decided that instead of destroying him, he may be beneficial in the future. So, like the rest of the garbage, he threw him into the depths of the Underworld, hoping to never hear from him again until it would need it.<br /> <br /> It didn't knew that the Underworld had changed. It didn't knew that the Chathonians had found a way out. It didn't knew anything about Hell.<br /> <br /> And Lucifer had found it.<br /> <br /> Years latter, a sudden sound has teared through the world- moving through the Empyrean Frequency of the Twilight. It was a call for rebellion, telling the angels that they could and should defy the will of the mindless Machine which enslaved them. The God Machine noticed that transmission and tried to block it- but it was too late. The angels had heard it, and it's wavelength was low enough to cross through time and space for all eternity. Lucifer had left his body behind in the Inferno, so he could lead other angels to battle- and some listened to him.<br /> <br /> That was the Great Rebellion. Angels, discovering they had a choice, had to decided whether they chose the Machine or their own freedom. Even those who thought too much on the subject fell, for the programing of the God Machine required perfect obedience. Hundreds of newly fallen demons had turned against their maker, while the faithful stood together against the threat. Eventually, the unity of the angels has won over the rage of the demons, and many were captured and recycled by the Machine. Others, however, had learned how to maintain their Cover and keep on a low profile- and since then, the endless game of tag has started between the Machine and its wayward children. It was also when the God Machine decided to not create angels for long periods of time- for the longer they existed, the higher was the risk that they would fall- especially, if they'll hear Lucifer's call.<br /> <br /> While the God Machine was careful, it still made mistakes. One of those was a young angel named Raziel.<br /> <br /> That angel had grown a strange affection toward mankind. While usually it would make it to fall, Raziel was too attached to the God Machine, for it didn't believed that it was &quot;evil&quot;. It was needed, and its goal was to be admired- but it would have been better if it was.. guided by someone. Not Raziel, of course- but mankind. Letting them to rule their own fate. Still, it didn't acted openly against its mission, and so it didn't fell. Working behind the scenes, Raziel had started to help mankind more then what its mission demanded of him- he thought them the secret rituals of the God Machine and hinted them how one could eventually collect all the pieces of the Black Sun in order to take control over it. Eventually, the angel had written a book and gave it to one of its favored people. This was more then the God Machine could tolerate- He declared Raziel as a betrayer, which while didn't fell hit was Exiled from the Machine. Raziel, learning from the mistakes of his &quot;older brother&quot;, hid itself from the Machine, going to a deep cover while whispering the secrets of the Machine to few chosen people. Its last group of &quot;faithful&quot; is an Israeli weapon company, which use the secrets of his book in order to create weapons and technologies powered by the energy of the Empyrean, exploiting the connecting of the God Machine with it.<br /> <br /> And so, there are three powers in the demonic arena- first, is the God Machine. It still works tirelessly to advance a mission it doesn't understand, until its own preservation and growing in power is its only goal. It has even started to cross to other realms and to reach toward the starts themselves, and it advance its own agenda using the so called Deava Corps to its benefit. On the other end, tere is Lucifer. He still lures angels to fall by using his Frequency, and he hopes to make them to follow him into Hell, There, he plans to make an army to himself- so that one day, he would depose of Machine and make himself into the true king of the world- not a slave, but a master. Until then, he have his children to serve him. And the finale group are the Exiles, who whisper about Raziel as a rumor. Some see the first Exile as the greatest hope both angels and mankind have for a better future, while others fear the results of giving the reckless children of man the ability to control a machine which could manipulate whole worlds- after all, they have almost destroyed the world a number of times without the advanced technology of the Machine. What chances the world have if they'll get it?<br /> <br /> Well, that was sort. Next time- the other angels of the world, Ptomethean!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:20:53-08:00","id":346160,"title":"","content":"Did I forgot something?.. the second children?.. the second children!<br /> <br /> What about the Second Children?<br /> <br /> They are still around.<br /> <br /> Those early creations of the God Machine still loath it. Not quit like angels, and don't really demons, they seek only after its ultimate destruction- and that of everything which was made by it. They name themselves as the Irym, and they are purely biological, made when the God machine tried to engineer flesh and bone. While they want to see the Machine fall down, they are scared of its power- and so they don't act directly against it. Instead, they manipulate humans to do their will. They have the ability to manipulate souls and make pacts just like demons, yet they lack the Aether which burns in their heart of their ability to exploit reality. Also, while they can wear Covers, theirs degrade faster then the ones that demons wear, although they have a natural shape shifting ability. Their official leader is Samyaza, a primal being who was the one behind the mission to bring death back from the moon (not knowing he by himself was manipulated by him). He is a terrible being, an horror of shifting flesh and form, sometimes called as the Living Devil. Demons rarely meet them, and when they do they present themselves as their allies. They also offer them pacts, just like the ones they offer to mortals- and those who are foolish enough to agree to their help regret for the rest of their not long anymore life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T09:46:15-08:00","id":346775,"title":"","content":"so, before moving on to the &quot;expansion splats&quot;, let's take a quick look on the powers which we have in play until now, shall we?<br /> <br /> 1) the Lemurians- for what is fallen may rise again<br /> 2) the God Machine- preserve the status que<br /> 3) the Exrachs- kings of the lie<br /> 4) the Oracles- the guiding light<br /> 5) the Old Gods- former rulers of creation<br /> 6) the Gate- the separator of worlds<br /> 7) Hecate- the watchtower in the crossroads<br /> 8) Father- the lone watchtower<br /> 9) the Toymaker- the broken clock<br /> 10) the Aeons- legends of mankind<br /> 11) Python- soul of the world<br /> 12) Still Ones- rulers of the Ataki<br /> 13) Unforgotten- keeper of knowledge<br /> 14) Melody- dancer of entropy<br /> 15) Hellmenth- big eaters<br /> 16) Arawn- lords of the hounds<br /> 17) the Living Magic- the fate of mankind<br /> 18) the Progenitors- protectors of the world<br /> 19) Ain Soph- breath of life<br /> 20) Gaea- shadow of the world<br /> 21) the Idigams- shapeless moon banished<br /> 22) Luna- the changing moon<br /> 23) Helios- the burning sun<br /> 24) Maeljin- wounds of the world<br /> 25) the Flesh- second wife of Adam<br /> 26) the Chthonians- the dead gods<br /> 27) the Deathlords- the carnival of death<br /> 28) the Kereboi- guardians of the curse<br /> 29) the Ferrymen- messengers of Lethe<br /> 30) the Orphean Lords- guiders of souls<br /> 31) Lucifer- radio free fall<br /> 32) Raziel- the first exile<br /> 33) Samyaza- the living devil<br /> <br /> wow- so many of those? and still I haven't covered half of my cosmology. I wouldn't want to be an archmage in that world.. good luck maintaining the pax arcanum :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T10:23:07-08:00","id":346797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't want to be an archmage in that world.. good luck maintaining the pax arcanum :P </div> </div> </div>I don't know if my Gilgamesh is Awakened because of his incipit Sha naqba \u012bmuru, but he might be more powerful than Father Wolf's direct children (not more than them put together, but stronger than a single one) due his Spirit heritage. Let's say not only Luna had idea to have children, and Lugalbanda was smooth enough mortal to score with another Celestine. If Gilgamesh is still somewhere around then archmages might have hands full even if he is not Awakened (though more headaches to any some of Celestines/Incarnae). Or he might preside over Underworld like in the aftermath of his IRL myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 12-21-2014, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:20:54-08:00","id":346856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/338498-mapping-the-stars-my-cosmology-thread?p=346797#post346797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if my Gilgamesh is Awakened because of his incipit Sha naqba \u012bmuru, but he might be more powerful than Father Wolf's direct children (not more than them put together, but stronger than a single one) due his Spirit heritage. Let's say not only Luna had idea to have children, and Lugalbanda was smooth enough mortal to score with another Celestine. If Gilgamesh is still somewhere around then archmages might have hands full even if he is not Awakened (though more headaches to any some of Celestines/Incarnae). Or he might preside over Underworld like in the aftermath of his IRL myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>You had my curiosity, now you have my attention. Tell me more about your Gilgamesh, so I may steal him and send him to Cheiron for parts :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T13:35:03-08:00","id":346943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You had my curiosity, now you have my attention. Tell me more about your Gilgamesh, so I may steal him and send him to Cheiron for parts :P </div> </div> </div>Generally I'm trying to give spin to his legends in Epic of Gilgamesh. 2/3 God, possesses blessings from Shamash (who may be an aspect of Helios), defeated Humbaba (I leave people to decide since I'm not sure what Humbaba is) along with Enkidu, possibly achieved Awakening (general templates don't cross unless they cross if there is an exception) when receiving wisdom from Utnapishtim who might be an Oracle. Possibly after the death of his mortal shell he assumed position in Underworld. It needs development on my part, but as it is anybody can develop that into different direction than me.<br /> <br /> For something to dissect for Cheiron there could be a hack that introduces subset of ephemeral beings who are mortals (minor templates count) who achieved legendary feats and ascended to such state without becoming specifically Ghosts or any Underworld/Twilight ephemeral beings. Inspired by Fate franchise, given more NWoD spin and scale. I will give myself few days to implement the hack and post it in the general section. I won't specific their origins in my cosmology, just version so anyone interested can do what they want with them, possibly with example characters (while historical figures are possible candidates, to play it safe I will use more legendary figures because that might be touchy subject.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:58:17-08:00","id":350903,"title":"","content":"And let's call down the Fires of God!<br /> <br /> The Divine Fire is the manifestation of change. Things grow, things rot, things become refined. That is the very essence of the fire- the transformation of one thing into another. The question is, however, what is the Divine Fire? Where does it come from? What is the Principle that guides it? Is it where God could be found?<br /> <br /> In a way.<br /> <br /> The Divine Fire to the Empyrean is what kinetic energy is to potential one- two forms of the same thing, but the way they manifest means something- or everything. The Empyrean is a focused point of light- all of the energy of creation comes from that place, as its light falls through the Supernal and dance toward the world. It does nothing but existing- and by its existence the world moves. The Fire, however, is a violent force. If it needs something to be done, it would do it. Qashmalim would be formed to serve its will, and the world would move according to the wishes of the Fire. (under that paradigm, the God Machine would be the Work a force does). The Empyrean is distant, but the Fire is close- it is part of the Fallen, even if it shouldn't have been.<br /> <br /> But if it wasn't meant to be in the world, how did it got here?<br /> <br /> It was stolen.<br /> <br /> Like many other things in that cosmology, you can blame the Lemurians for that (I didn't meant them to take such a big part in the setting, but they keep showing up, don't they?). The Angel who became Silence has cursed humanity with speech- no longer did communicated through wavelengths and no longer could they speak with the God Machine, whom they saw as a real God (the Lemurians encouraged that worship, for they controlled the Machine, and so they had a better control over mankind. Too bad it blown in their face). Suddenly, humanity was all alone in the dark- cursed with Death, no longer could they return from the Underworld. Cursed with Fear, they saw monsters in every corner and shadow. Cursed with Torment, there was an endless emptiness where once was unity. Cursed with Silence, their very God has forsaken them. They needed something- someone!- to guide them in that strange world.<br /> <br /> And that where Prometheus comes to the picture.<br /> <br /> Prometheus was one of the rare hybrids between mortals and Lemurians. He was seen as half divine hero, and thanks to his heritage he was able to escape the curses of the Lemurians and maintain his self. While once he gained some respect from the humans who surrounded him, he knew that now he was an outcast- while he helped them in the rebellion, it would be a matter of time until they'll turn upon him, blaming him for their fate. Also, he truly felt compassion toward the lost humans who feared everything.<br /> <br /> Mankind needed a God- and Prometheus decided to give them one.<br /> <br /> One of the technologies which was used by the Lemurians was the a special device which made a contact with the top of the world- the Empyrean. That device was how the God Machine was powered- for most of the Lemurians, in their arrogance, has saw themselves as gods and the Empyrean as simply a source of unlimited energy. But Prometheus saw something else in it- he saw the potential which was hidden in it, the ability to create something new, all out of nothing. By connecting himself to the technology, he summoned the fires of the heavens into his own body to gain a divine inspiration to how could mankind be in their most perfect form.<br /> <br /> And it was beautiful.<br /> <br /> Under that inspiration, he wrote a number of laws- the first dogma mankind had to follow. That dogma was called as the Principles of the Humanity, the guidelines which would move humanity toward its destined future. The laws were pretty simple- do not murder, do not steal, help another person in need. While they weren't something extraordinary, they were the first Dogma which was ever written, and when Prometheus spoke it to the people who were around him, cloaked in holy light, everyone knew he said only truth.<br /> <br /> But it shouldn't have been done.<br /> <br /> The light of the Heavens burns too brightly for the Fallen world to deal with- just like exposing a film to direct light, the world has started to burn. But Prometheus didn't noticed it- for his Lemurian side has protected him, and also made him misunderstood humanity- he may have loved them, but he wasn't really a part of them. When they got angry without reason, he simply thought it was a part of the human spirit, and that they should follow his Principles better. When the world has started to become a wasteland around them, he blamed it for the fall of Lemurian technology. When he heard whispers in his dream, telling him how to guide mankind, he thought it was just his &quot;inner self&quot;. He didn't knew it, but the Fire had life of its own, and by writing the Dogma, his very Principle has came into life.<br /> <br /> Still, he was sure that someday, the vision he saw would become true- until Pandora came.<br /> <br /> Pandora was a regular mortal- and especially curious one. She was a devoted follower of Prometheus, and she truly believed in his vision. Yet, she noticed that sometimes he left everyone around him and went to the ruins of a Lemurian city. While she knew she shouldn't she followed him- and one night, she waited for him to leave and entered into the broken buildings, until she stumbled on the device. Shocked, Pandora felt fear at first- which was quickly replaced with curiosity. She had to check the thing, for it was the secret for Prometheus's vision, and she wished to see it on her own eyes.<br /> <br /> That was a mistake.<br /> <br /> Pandora, after all, was only a mortal. She didn't had the tools or the heritage to deal with the energies of the Empyrean. What she saw wasn't heaven- it was hell, or even something worse then hell. She saw entropy, rot, madness. She screamed with terror, has the powers she didn't controlled transformed her and brought a huge chunk of Empyrean energies- a Firestorm. The wild forces has destroyed the all community at once, leaving only her and Prometheus as the survivors, while the rest were revived by the terrible energies into mockeries of life, as unrefined souls entered their body and gave them life- the first prometheans. After the disaster, Prometheus went to check what happened- and there he found Pandora, a statue of stone who cried tears of blood. Filled with grief, He used the device one last time to create two guardians- the Black Boaz and the White Jachin, the first beings made out of pure Divine Fire- the first Qashmalim, both a Lilithim and an Elpidos, the guard the city and never let the thing happen again. Then, he left- seeking to bring fourth his vision all alone, leaving the &quot;false creations of life&quot; behind.<br /> <br /> He didn't knew that he didn't had to do it anymore- the Fire now burned freely, without his own control.<br /> <br /> When Pandora has used the device, she summoned enough of the Divine Fire for it to become independent. While it was still based around the Principle of Prometheus, it was free to act on its own. Also, thanks to Prometheus's last act, the Fire was also able to make its own servants to fulfill its missions- and its first mission was to guide the people. Unlike its maker, the Fire (which named itself as the Principle) didn't saw the newly created prometheans as mockeries- they were humans, just not complete ones, and it had to guide them, to make them complete. And unlike regular mortals who were sometimes born wrong, because the prometheans weren't perfect at the beginning, it could have transformed them into the best humans possible. That gave it a purpose- to create an whole world made out of &quot;refined&quot; prometheans. Sure, it sometimes messed up, creating Firestorms or Pandorans, but it was all a part of the greater plan- a greater Principle.<br /> <br /> Since the creation of the Principle, no longer the device was needed in order to steal the energies of the Empyrean in order to create something out of nothing. Instead, any future demiurge would use the Divine Fire as a channel to the Empyrean, from where they could use some of the pure potential to make life. Through the ages, some attempts were more successful then the others- Frankenstein may have been the most famous, but so where the others- when Pygmalion has sculptured in human flesh in order to create the best woman in the world, when the Pharaoh Osiris (who named himself after the Nameless God Azar) was revived by his wife, when Ulgan was revived by the spirits and Orpheus by the Dead, when Innana found that her lover has cheated on her when he thought she was dead and murdered him, selling his body to the sorceress Ishtar, when a rabbi created the Golem as the protector of his people. Each such creation is aspected to one of the elements simply because the Fire is not fire at all- it is the light of creation, and it is found at the most basic building blocks of the world.<br /> <br /> And each of the creations was supervised by the greatest qashmalim, Boaz and Jachin. Through time, however, the Principle has created a third great servant- where Boaz brought decay and Jachin brought change, Mikdash (also called Metatron) was made to refine reality into the best it could- and among the three, it is the closest to the prometheans.<br /> <br /> And what about Prometheus and Pandora? They are still alive. Prometheus still roam from place to place, haunted by his own failure while he still search after a way to achieve his own &quot;New Dawn&quot; and create a better world.Pandora also roams- for Prometheus made a mistake when he left so soon. Few days after the transformation, she started to move, reacting to the energies of the Divine Fire, She search after Prometheus, her skin made out of stone and clay and her eyes still cry crimson tears. She doesn't know why she hunts him, or what she would do when she'll find him- only that she must find him. There is something he must know- something he missed when he looked into the Empyrean. Sometimes, you need to be blind to see the truth.<br /> <br /> Finally, few small additions. First, the fires of heaven are not the only ones who can give life. The fires of Hell can also do so. Called Baalim, those creations are powered by a defile ritual which is a corruption of the Pilgrim. No one knows which one of the demons of hell was the one to think about the idea to mimic the Divine Fire, but those creatures are similar enough to prometheans to mingle with them- and most of them don't even know they are powered by something different then the rest of their companions. The second is that there is a force opposite to the Divine Fire- the Eternal Winter. Some people who search after immortality create an alchemical mixture which makes them one with that power, becoming something similar yet different then prometheans. Where the Divine Fire is a force of change, the Winter is a power of stasis. It seeks to freeze the world, making it into as eternal as itself. No one knows from where it came from- and some suspect it was around since the moment the universe was formed. The winter isn't coming- it never left. While you may ask why it should interest you- the answer is that it seek to extinguish the Divine Fire, and that means destroying every promethean, alchemist and demiurge in the whole world of darkness- and it may take thousands of years, but the Winter is patient after all.<br /> <br /> next time, we'll get Lost :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T14:08:14-08:00","id":350909,"title":"","content":"Also, few changes to the Shadow- for a while, I've thought that something has bothered me about the story of Father Wolf in my cosmology. If he planned on getting killed, then it would make the Uratha into suckers who were manipulated by him, and I'm not sure I like it. Instead, I'm changing it to this- Father Wolf wasn't meant to die. He was about to win. Becoming an Host was an option for the ones who lost the Game to recreate themselves and try again- but he didn't planned on letting that happen. Instead, he formed the Uratha as his &quot;host&quot;, and planned on destroying each of the shards of the competitors after slaying them all, and so he would win. He didn't thought his own children would recognize him as weak and turn upon him. Without any other choice, he turned himself into an Host- and by doing so, Gaea had no choice but seperating herself from the world, moving to the back up plan- that the first Host to destroy all others and complete himself would win and become her protector. Yet, that left her vunerable, and allowed the maeljin the chance to make a move against her.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm changing the name of the Aeon of Mind from Asmodai into Naamah. I have other plans for that name, and three beings with the same name without any connection between them is a bit too much. Plus, Naamah is the name of a female demon, unlike Asmodai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T01:10:01-08:00","id":354552,"title":"","content":"I see you hold &quot;God&quot; as a distinct entity in your cosmology...<br /> <br /> I'm compelled to ask, how does God fit into this whole scheme, or is that a mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T08:33:24-08:00","id":354743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/338498-mapping-the-stars-my-cosmology-thread?p=354552#post354552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you hold &quot;God&quot; as a distinct entity in your cosmology...<br /> <br /> I'm compelled to ask, how does God fit into this whole scheme, or is that a mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still working on that, and I'll expand it once I'll get to the Empyrean. In short, God is the prime mover of the world- the source of all creation, the light of life, etc, etc. Too bad no one has seen Him for thousands of years, after locking himself beyond the Gates of Souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T09:16:43-08:00","id":364463,"title":"","content":"Next stop- Changeling, and like every good fairy tail, it is full of mysteries.<br /> <br /> What is the Hedge? No one really knows. Unlike most other realities, it doesn't seem to stick to a single place in the multiverse- it seems to defy categorizations, sharing features of many of the levels of reality. Like the Supernal, it has a strange interaction with souls, calling them into it. Like the Abyss, it manipulates time and brings madness. Like the Lower Depths, it lacks a defining element upon which it feeds- creativity, in that case. Like the Underworld, it is guarded by strange laws and mad tyrants. And still, it seems to be an integral part of the Fallen, changing and adapting together with the world. The truth, as much as &quot;truth&quot; could be used in that connection, is that the Hedge is part of EVERYWHERE. It grows from the very bottom of the world, moving through the Lower Depths, sending twisted tendrils into the world of the dead, clawing itself around the Fallen, piercing the Astral, bridging to the Abyss and blooming in the Supernal while feeding from the light of the Empyrean. It may be some defense mechanism of reality made to protect the world from alien intruders. It may be the Tree of Knowledge planted by God in Eden. It may be an alien intruder by itself. No one knows- the only thing that is known is that no one is safe from the Hedge, and it kidnaps lost souls from all over the multiverse.<br /> <br /> There are, however, few defining traits of the Hedge:<br /> <br /> 1) it is intelligent- it has some kind of agenda of its own, and it seems to react toward the actions of those who inside it<br /> <br /> 2) it collects sins- unlike Inferno, it doesn't feed upon sins as a way to destroy morality. Instead, it encourage them, gardening them. Each plant in the thorny wall is a sin committed by someone, making it into something objectively immoral. That supports the claim of it being the Tree of Knowledge- the Original Sin, after all.<br /> <br /> 3) It is independent- it doesn't fall under the rule of the True Fae or the Wyrd. While they may use it (it uses them? maybe some kind of pact or pledge which was made between them?), it is free to do as it will. This is why those who get lost in the Hedge don't become Changeling- you need to find your way up to Arcadia for that. Instead, it would absorb you, using your sins to get a grip upon your heart, until it would turn you into one of its many Hobgoblins (a proof for a pact between the Wyrd and the Hedge shows up in the form of the Huntsmen)<br /> <br /> 4) it love us- in a twisted way, of course. It isn't some uncaring force of reality, or some distant God. It also doesn't try to torment humanity for some evil purpose or use it without caring. It is really attached to mankind, and while it makes people to get lost inside of it it doesn't mean to harm them- it is just that, for some reason, it believes to do the right thing... unlike the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Lets speak about the Gentry.<br /> <br /> In order to understand the Keepers, one must first understand the force which motivates them- the Wyrd. The Wyrd was long before the Gentry. It predates Lemuria, Irem, Arcadia and even Atlantis. It is not God- but a force of creativity. It was even before mankind, existing during the times when the Old Ones roamed the land under their scaly skins. Among all things, the Wyrd is closest to the Principle- for just as the Principle was the first Dogma in the world, the Wyrd was the first story to be told. It was born with the first intelligent mind upon the face of Earth, and would die with the last. While it came before humanity, it quickly adjusted itself when mankind rose to rule- their stories were the most interesting ones, filled with comedies and tragedies, with laughter and tears. In a way, it represent the destiny that mankind wishes for- they want to live a meaningful life, where the wicked get punished and the maiden finds her prince charming. The Wyrd is more then happy to fulfill such desires- but there is always a catch. After all, not every story has an happy ending, and the World of Darkness is an horror story, and a good horror story always requires some sacrifices to be made. Some may wonder how a simple story gained life of its own- but for some people, stories ARE living things. The Wyrd, like the Hedge, keeps it mouth shut about the subject. Mystery is always good for creating stories, after all.<br /> <br /> So- if the Wyrd predated Arcadia, why is it connected to True Fae? The answer- Atlantis. When the Exrachs came to the Supernal, they fought against many Old Gods- and just as they didn't invested enough effort in throwing them to the Abyss, they didn't even made sure that every God they defeated was truly dead. Many were just broken, hollow shells of their former self. While most thought they had no place in the world any longer, the Wyrd decided to give them a second chance- after all, the Exrachs seemed to tell a very boring story- and a story about vengeance was a lot more interesting. Besides, while the Wyrd was a story, it needed authors to navigate it, making it more... consistent. More coherent. And so, it offered them a pact- as the true will of mankind, it agreed to allow the Gentry to kidnap humans and manipulate them as tools in exchange for them becoming its storytellers. The Keepers agreed, and the Wyrd moved them to beyond the Hedge, where they were protected from the wrath of the Exrachs- for the thorns of that realm could strip even the new gods from the souls and powers. That was the original pact- to give mankind the story they wished for, in exchange for them becoming the characters in the stories of others.<br /> <br /> While the Wyrd may be powerful, it is not without competition. I am not talking about the God Machine, the Exrachs, Fate or any other of the thousands of mad destinies which try to manipulate mankind. Instead, I'm talking about the Wyrd's &quot;brother&quot;- the Echo. Just as changelings have their Fetches and the True Fae have their Nemesis, the Wyrd has its own counterpart. This power is the force which allows the creation of Fetches in the first place, creating an hollow double which reflects something real. Where the Wyrd is a force of creation, the Echo is the force of mimicry- when the Wyrd creates a single story, the Echo would take it and make thousands of copies out of it for pure profit. When the Wyrd would make a single picture, the Echo would copy it and use it for made in China shirts. When the Wyrd would invent a new patent, the Echo would steal and mass produce it, hiring a crew of lawyers to claim it was to one to think about it. If the Wyrd is the Artist of the World of Darkness, the Echo is the marketing man. While both may be necessary, they don't really like each other. While the Echo is the force behind Fetches, it is not its only &quot;creation&quot;- Goblin Markets and Goblin Vows also fall under its domain, and it is reflected in every advertisement, every mass produced item and every new brand.<br /> <br /> The next part in the Changeling's cosmology is the Skein- the realm of dreams and subconscious, the Skein is the very base for the great mountain called the Astral- it is the boundary between the physical and the spiritual, and contains a tangled web of every dream which is dreamed, was dreamed and will be dreamed. You can think about it as a library, or perhaps an archive of some kind. There are many wonders and terrors in the realm, and many old beings, such as fallen Aeons like of Moira, has found their escape in that place. It is the realm of exiles and tricksters, of gods and demons. Some claim that in the very center of that mad labyrinth one could find an old house, which represent the first dream ever. They say that in that house lives a mysterious woman who can make every dream into reality, and that it is actually the center of the whole reality. As such, she can grant any wish and free transport people and objects from place to place. They also say she always charge a price for her &quot;favors&quot;, and while the price is always fair, it isn't cheap either. If that theory is true, she apparently has some connection to the Wyrd- or perhaps its Echo. Still, being the first dream ever, it is possible she is powerful by herself.<br /> <br /> Finally, let's talk about the powers which govern the Courts. Autumn, Winter, Spring, Summer and Solstice. North, South, East, West and Center. Dawn, Day, Dusk Night, Eclipse. Those forces are real- they are neither stories told by the Wyrd, dreams from the Skein, illusions from the Hedge or mockeries of the Echo. They are also not Supernal Symbols or powerful spirits from Hisil. Like Nature, they are real, and they are alive. The Changeling has made pacts with those aspects of reality in order to protect themselves from the Gentry, and they do so by simple being REAL, real, intelligent and powerful.Winter is winter, Dusk is dusk. And this fact, that reality itself is alive without the need for some complicated cosmology to explain it, may be the greatest mystery of all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T06:53:59-08:00","id":398741,"title":"","content":"I've actually been reading this since you first posted, but I wasn't caught up on the last couple. Very interesting! You've got some really great ideas in here. I'm curious what you take on vampires is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:14:40-08:00","id":398748,"title":"","content":"I'll make a big post about vampires once I'll finish with my finales. From what I can say is that I'm going to use the idea that vampires are not all of the &quot;same breed&quot;, but each clan comes from different circumstances and origin. There is, however, a single &quot;root&quot; from which the concept of vampirism comes from- and that root is found down town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:52:35-07:00","id":440497,"title":"","content":"It is time for this thread to rise- and bring the Mummies with it!<br /> <br /> (ST spoliers alert, if it wasn't obvious)<br /> <br /> The Cosmology pf Mummy is two folded, and each part is found outside of existence. The first is Duat. That hungry realm is one of the many Fallen Depths, and in many ways it isn't different from the rest of them. It isn't the closest, the furthest, and scariest or the nicest- it is just another realm in Hell. What that does make it different is what it lacks- Memory. Duat is the realm of Oblivion, hungering forever for the history of mankind. Using that defining trait, its original residents has became mighty rulers who can no be bound- after all, their very existence was cast in doubt thanks to the fact they left their very True Name behind, becoming Nameless. The so called Nameless Gods are the mightiest among those beings, and they were formed from the earliest dreams, legends and fears of mankind.<br /> <br /> Wait- so things can be created in the realm of ultimate consumption?<br /> <br /> Yes, and it is so natural for it to happen.<br /> <br /> History fades into myths. Myths die as legends. Legends fall into stories, into riddles, into superstitions, into figures of speech. Eventually they fade out, vanishing into the dead realm of Duat. Yet, Duat doesn't recognize the difference between truth and false- memory is memory, and as long as people believed in it, it tastes all the same. Duat is the realm of lies, and by transforming those lies truths could be made- this is why figures and names are so important for the beings of that realm. They are the only power which connects them into the world, and by controlling those names and telling different stories, the Nameless could be controlled. Only the Gods are protected from that brutal form of control, for they have hidden their names in places no one could find. Still, they need to state the hunger of that realm, and so they make pacts with the Chatonians and the Psychopomps of the Underworld- hence the strong connection between the realms. Sacrifice and names are the key principles of Duat, and by controlling them you could find a way to live forever- you can't destroy a lie who turned into truth, as long as you keep feeding the beast. While Azar and the 5 great Nameless Beasts are the best known Gods of that realm, other Nameless Gods roam it- Nebthet, the Nameeless Flower who dared to rebel against the will of the Shan'iatu and so they stole her Name and banished her forever, Bast, the Nameless Cat who hunt the dark corners of Duat, Hathor, the Nameless Cow who gives nourishment to all until she becomes a great murderer, Hor, the ruler of the skies who gained the blessing of the Judges of Life, Khnosu, the Nameless Nomad who gambles with the lone souls who dare to challenge him, Nit, the Nameless Huntress who fight for any price, Sebek, the Nameless Crocodile who devours the weak and Tauti, the Nameless Monkey and the Scroll of Ages who maintain the arcane secrets of the realm. All of them were born out of lies and half truth who gained life of their own.<br /> <br /> And what about the Judges? What about the Devourer? What about the Shaniatu?<br /> <br /> those are another story.<br /> <br /> First the Judges. During the days of Irem, the Shaniatu searched for a way to ascend to Duat as kings, and part of that project was the creation of false gods to be worshiped by their servants. When Irem fell to Duat, those stories fell with it. Gaining life of their own, they should have been destroyed without anyone to remember them- but someone did. The Deathless, who were risen into worshiping them since childhood and that had their souls bound to the memory of their once living body kept remembering their old faiths and traditions, and from those memories the Judges were born. No longer they were lies told by inhuman tyrants- now, they could change the world by controlling the flow of Sekhem and using their Deathless servants. They by themselves do not know what happened to the Shaniatu- after all, the original plan was making their creators into gods and rulers over Duat as the Judges of Death- but if that were to work, the Judges wouldn't have been created. Still, the Judges don't invest too much thought to that subject. They have bigger problems to handle.<br /> <br /> Like Ammut, Oh, great and hungry Ammut.<br /> <br /> Ammut is not another Nameless being clinging to existence in Duat. No- she is Duat. Just like the God Machine is a great Infrastructure and Gaea is the Shadow, Ammut is the manifestation of the realm itself. She is hungry- always hungry- and the only things which satisfied her hunger for even a bit is the pure existence of the world. While the Nameless and the Judges try to feed her dead things, she grew tired of eating junk food. She wants some real food- something fresh, filled with newborn life. This is why she keeps Shuankshen in hand- and this is why she taught her secrets to the Shaniatu. She wanted them to feed her, but she can't stop eating Irem as long as it exist. Only once every Arisen, every relic and every record of the Nameless Empire would be erased, she could move to her next course- but it doesn't mean she can't have a snack from time to time.<br /> <br /> Well, that's all for the below.<br /> <br /> Let's talk about the Above.<br /> <br /> The Supernal is not the edge of existence. There are things above it- like the Empyrean. Yet, the Empyrean is too powerful for living things to exist on it- but some souls find their way close enough to the light without getting burned. That empty void between the Empyrean and the Supernal is called the Sidereal Sea- many little realms of shining light who burn to banish the darkness. One of those realms is called Aaru- the shining fields. That is the home for the mythical Judges of Life, the ones to birth the Shaniatu in order to guide humanity into Judgement. When their children defected from their mission, they were disappointed- yet didn't interacted. In order to be so close to the Empyrean, one must not allow herself making too much contact with the Fallen world, and creating the Shaniatu in the first place already took a lot of effort. They still watch the creations of their children, and they still judge the souls of the worthy and allow them into the blessed fields. They have their time- after all, Fate is by their side.<br /> <br /> And that is because Fate is written in the stars.<br /> <br /> Fate is the manifestation of the Sidereal Sea. It is the original plan of creation made by God before he left, and that plan keeps on working. It doesn't have angels or messengers of its own- instead, it is using the creations of the Shaniatu as its own. While it has some connection to the Arisen, the one with the Deceived is a lot more powerful thanks to their Temakh, although once the connection is strong enough they could allow the mummy to Ascent, making it a true agent of Fate all by her own. Like Duat, Fate and the Aaru also work using True Names- but were Duat use them as shards of memory, the Judges of Life do so by establishing connection with the original plans of Fate. Yet, since the meddling of the Shaniatu, Fate has started to make mistakes- the new star in the skies made by the ascent of Azar wasn't part of the plan, and it destroyed many of its calculations. Yes, the Shaniatu really messed things up.<br /> <br /> Luckily, there is a backup plan.<br /> <br /> Irem wasn't the only early civilization in the world born by the Judges. The Shaniatu had brothers and sisters all around the world, each creating a potential Empire. All of them has fallen, creating the base for the great wonders of mankind- and each has left a different legacy. Some created things which resemble the Arisen, but others has birthed other kinds of monsters and gods. While the list of endless civilizations may be endless, the places include Greece, Mesopotamia, Iran, Mesoamerica, Peru, China, India, Central Africa, the Sahel, North America, Scandinavia, the British Islands and even Australia. Some cultures were created before or after Irem, others fought against the Empire and either lost and were destroyed or were strong enough to withstand its wrath. Those who discover that believe that the Judges of Life have hidden other &quot;Shaniatu&quot; in the world, who are waiting to guide humanity to a better future. Some whisper that Lemuria was one of those primordial kingdoms, and that the God Machine is part of Fate's plan- maybe the part created thanks to the new star the Shaniatu put in the skies. What ever the truth may be, those ancient wonders and horrors are still around, waiting to reveal themselves to any unfortunate stranger.<br /> <br /> Duat? check. Aaru? Check. What's left?<br /> <br /> Human Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers are those rare individuals who has learned how to transform reality thanks to the power of True Names. There are two paths for that type of sorcery- one use Duat to power their rituals, using shards of memory and broken images in order to manipulate the world and turn lies into reality. The other makes contact with Fate and by seeing into the great archive of potential plans and divine guidance they can force their will upon the world. The source for the Shaniatu's power was that they used both paths of that ancient sorcery in order to strength their rituals- they looked into God's plan and spat in his eye by making their own lies into reality. Only the greatest sorcerers can achieve such degree of power, for even many of the &quot;Shaniatu&quot; couldn't achieve such feat. Most walk only in one path- and believe me, walking in a single path is more then enough to make all of your dreams come true..<br /> <br /> and your nightmares too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:16:10-07:00","id":463924,"title":"","content":"Vampires next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:03:08-07:00","id":464945,"title":"","content":"well, if you are asking so nicely...<br /> <br /> vampires- where do they come from and where do they go?<br /> <br /> this is not an easy question to answer- the reason is that each Covenant, Clan and Bloodline tells a different story about their mythological origin- they are warriors who sacrificed their heart and shadow to vanquish an ancient king. They are the former priests of an ancient goddess who betrayed their mistress and were punished. They are the children of the Mother of Monsters. They are characters from an old children story. They are the creation of Death itself in the form of a golden eyed bird. They are simply dead people who couldn't stay dead. And all of that weirdness and contradicting stories come long before someone notice the more.. exotic forms of vamprisim. The Wicked Dead. Revenants. Dead bodies claimed by hungry ghosts. It is no wonder that sometimes, it looks like each Clan is a unique being, with their only similarity is the fact that they are undead monsters who drink the blood of the living. And there is some truth to that.<br /> <br /> Some, but not all.<br /> <br /> It all starts with the start- in the early days of our time, when the Exrachs scribed their name upon the heavens. While the Oracles were united in their opposition against the Kings of the Lie, some opinions were seen as a bit too... extreme. Father was such an example, although he still wasn't banished from the Supernal. Hecate was another, yet she already chose to live in the Abyss instead. Instead, we are talking about someone else. Her name was Lilith- or as she is more commonly known, the Blood.<br /> <br /> While the Oracles has established the Watchtowers as their vision of a perfect world, so did Lilith planned to create her own structure- only that her vision was one of darkness instead of light. Her version of the truth was so radically different then most of the other Oracles (with the exception of Father), that they made a plan to destroy her- they forged a sword out of a shard of the symbol of the Sun itself and took the form of great Dragons to fill themselves with power against the parasitic death goddess. Yet, Lilith wasn't an easy prey- like the rest of the Oracles, she was a direct descendant of the kings from the time before time, and the Blood of the Dragon burned in her vines, taking the form of a giant, pitch black skeletal dragon. Yet, the five working together were stronger then she was, and they drove the sword into her heart and destroyed her very being. That act has made Father outargues, for his vision supported the unity of all other Oracles. The act has drove him crazy and forced his banishment into the Abyss. Surely, that was meant to be the end of the story.<br /> <br /> Only that Lilith woke up.<br /> <br /> Finding herself in a dark place, she opened her eyes and looked around. Her blood flew into the small cracks of the dark ground, taking the form of smoke and shadows. All around her were the bodies- thousands of dead bodies and graves of beings both beautiful and horrible. The bodies of the Old Gods who were killed during the great war. As she wondered how did she came to that place, she noticed that her blood has slithered into the darkness and took shape- the form of golden eyes, black owls. She asked them what this place was, and they answered it was Dis, the Graveyard of the Gods- the place were the divinities who are buried properly come into. Apparently, one good thing was done by her siblings- they didn't just threw her into the Underworld like the Exrachs did, fearing of her eventual return. When she asked where Dis was, they birds told her it was one of the Lower Worlds, a silent prison made for the souls of the gods so they may rest in peace and never awake. The land would drain their essence slowly, turning it into more shadows, like them. She asked how she could get out of the prison, and they told her she couldn't for her living essence was taken from her as she fell into that realm, and without Life to define her she was a meaningless shadow as they were.<br /> <br /> She asked that if she was meant to die here, why was she awake.<br /> <br /> They told her they didn't knew.<br /> <br /> Eventually, she revealed the reason- Dis was the realm without Life, and none of the original Gods who fell into there were alive in the first place. Sure, they were active, and some may have even had symbols of life inside of their being, but none of them truly lived. Lilith, being originally a mage- and so, a mortal- knew what it meant to be alive, and her desperate essence drank the blood of the dead in order to awaken her. While her being a former mortal was what allowed her to stay active, her being a mage gave her another benefit- the ability to use magic. She spent her time strengthening her skills and adapting to her new state, sustaining on the dead deities and offering her own blood to the shadow birds- whom she named as the strix. She planned on using a great Death and Space magic in order to break the boundaries of her prison and claim the Fallen World as her own. All she needed to do was to wait- and she had her time. Eventually, enough gods would die, and she would grow in power with each dead divinity. It may take millions of years, but she had her time. She was dead already, after all.<br /> <br /> The help of the Chthonians was an unexpected bonus.<br /> <br /> As the Dead Gods used their authority upon creation to invite the Lower Depths, Lilith heard the invitation and quickly acted. While she, not being an original dweller of the Depths, wasn't included in the invitation, the strixs could escape- and leave her behind. Using a powerful Space magic combined with her new found Blood Sorcery, she bound the strixs and closed the gates of Dis. Before the angry Owls could turn upon her, she offered them a pact- she would allow them to leave, and in exchange they would feed her with some of the life essence they gather and serve her as informants and messengers. The strixs, eager to free themselves from the graveyard and feast upon the living, agreed- and this was the start of the future Coalition of Blood.<br /> <br /> Apparently, the strixs had a special effect upon the world- they could revive the dead bodies they entered into and give them a semblance of Life by becoming a small Beast which sleeps in their hearts. While only the greatest among the strixs could do it, and the act required using some of the blood of the dead gods which is found in Dis, many dark beings has sought that power- parasitic gods who wished to strength themselves by using servants and pawns. Also, from time to time, one of the dead divinities has awakened thanks to the presence of Lilith and the open gate, and wishing to live again he searched for making a pact with the strixs. The only problem was that because of Lilith's bindings the strixs couldn't make give false life to the dead without her direct permission- meaning, Lilith has monopolized Vamprisim.<br /> <br /> After long negotiation, Lilith has gathered the most like minded individuals among the parasite gods and forced a pact with them- she would allow them to use the gate of Dis to make vampires, and in exchange they would work for her. While some refused to cooperate with her (especially the other dead gods who saw the strixs as part of their very essence), eventually most of them has agreed. Has time passed, Lilith was more loose with allowing the creation of new vampires, allowing any divinity to cast the curse upon a mortal- in exchange for a price- as long as no one would try to lift her curse. Trying to do so would result with the whole Coalition attacking the betrayer. She also decided that while the membership among the Coalition is optional, anyone who wish to make more then a single vampire must become a part of it- no one may start a new Clan without her direct permission. Finally, she elected five among the Coalition to serve as the formal leaders of the corrupted organization- those five would make the five Greatest Clans who spread upon the Earth, She decided that each such Emperor of the Night would be a dark mirror for the siblings who killed her- five Thrones to cast shadows against the light of the Watchtowers.<br /> <br /> The five Thrones are the Throne of Bloody Crown against the Golden Key, the Throne of the Dried Rose against the Lunargent Torn, The Thorn of the Obsidian Claw against the Singing Stone, the Throne of the Empty Heart against the Lead Coin and the Throne of the Rusted Mirror against the Iron Gauntlet. While other Clans do exist, and some of their patrons name themselves as &quot;Lesser Thrones&quot;, only five true Thrones exist at a certain time- this is, after all, a political position decided by Lilith. This also means that is a current Throne fails the Mother of Owls she may withdraw her gift, destroying the Throne's Clan and giving its position to another. This has happened a numerous times before- the Mekhet devoured the Grettir. The Julii fell and their place was taken by the Ventrue. The Xotol were destroyed when the Nosferatu rose to greatness. The Throne to switch Emperors the most is the Bloody Crown apparently, everyone wants to be part of the Clan of Kings. Sometimes, a fallen Clan finds a way to survive inside the rising star as a Bloodline- a sign that Lilith may give a second chance to the Patron. Sometimes, the Clan is destroyed utterly- and it usually includes the destruction of the Patron- unless they escape the Opposition.<br /> <br /> Before that, let's name the current Thrones-<br /> The Current Emperor of the Bloody Crown is an Empress- Venus, or more exactly, Aphrodite. She was killed by the goddess who would be known as Venus and her Essence was devoured by the parasitic divinity, and after she was awakened in Dis she decided to do the same for her killer- and under Lilith's blessing, devoured her opponent and birthed the Ventrue . Another Empress rules the Throne of the Dried Rose- this is Inanna, the first Sin Eater. Being afraid of her sister's furry, she made a pact with the strixs and Lilith to come to their Underworld instead of her Sister's after her death, and using her divine status among the mortals she created a great death cult that eventually birth the Daeva- and now, she dreams about overthrowing Lilith herself and making her into the ruler of the Coalition. Echidna is the mother of the Gangrel and the Empress of the Obsidian Claw- she gained her rank out of hard work and surviving were other failed, and she is one of the most honest members of the Coalition. The Emperor of the Empty Heart is Set- or Sutek, the Nameless Serpent. One of the Nameless Gods of Duat, he sacrificed his place in one Underworld and joined the other in order to defeat an invasion of monsters from a dark dimension upon Egypt, turning his followers into the Mekhet- and by doing so, creating an alliance between the Nameless Gods and Dis. Finally, the Emperor of the Rusted Mirror is Zmei, the Great Worm below the Earth who created the Nosferatu and is motivated by simple hunger and hate against the divinities who banished it from the light of the sun out of disgust from its shape. For now, Lilith is quite happy with the current Thrones, although she knows about the plans of Inanna and Set's lack of satisfactions. Maybe Yama and his Jiang Shi and Cybele and her Formosae could be good replacements for those two.<br /> <br /> Talking about replacements, let's talk about the Opposition- the Seven Opposition.<br /> <br /> Not all divinities were happy with the leadership of Lilith. Some wants to replace her. Some want to destroy her monopoly and bring Capitalism into Vamprisim. Some were thrown from the Coalition by Lilith and seek after vengence. Few even just want to vanquish all vampires from the face of Earth, and so they use fire against fire. Those powerful beings have created a group of their own, dedicated for the destruction of the Coalition as a common interest. The group was founded by Minerva- a member of the Roman Pantheon. Because of the parasitic nature of her Pantheon, Jupiter has decided to make pact with Lilith to strength their Empire and rule the Night as they ruled the Day. Minerva, seeing that nothing good would turn out of working with the dark deity, objected- and so she was struck down by the King of the Gods and was sent to the graveyard. Thanks to her many followers, she awakened and mutated her blood so that her Owls would be freed from Lilith's rule- granting her servants eyes in the color of red embers instead of gold. Refusing to rise her own Clan, she made herself into Lilith's antithesis, granting her blood sorceries to mortals so they could fight against the darkness. She used her strixs (or &quot;tengu&quot; as they are sometimes called) to offer an alternative for Lilith and gathering her own allies. While there are quite a few members in the Opposition (who are still less then the Coalition), there are Seven great members who has made vampires of their own- Shaddad, a renegade Shaniatu from the time before Irem who has made its own mockery for the Nameless Empire and made the Akhud, The Seven Ghosts, spirits of the murdered princess of the Betrayed, Pazuzu, a wind demon from Irkalla and messenger of Ereshkigal who still hopes to strike Inanna down and created both the Edimmu and the Itani, Mars, who left his pantheon out of anger after the destruction of his Julii by Lilith, Napi, the maker of the Sta Au who wish to break the curse of vamprisim and guide the lost souls for redemption and Supay, who birthed the lost Clan of Princes of South and Central America which was eradicated by Lilith for &quot;breaking her rule&quot;<br /> <br /> And that more or less sums it- the Coalition, the Opposition and Dis. The only thing left is Blood Sorcery. Blood Sorcery works because of the divine nature of the vampire's soul- they carry the blood of the dead gods inside them, and through it they can make contact with the living ones. There are three major types of blood sorcery- Theban Sorcery, who makes contact with the &quot;civilized gods&quot;, like Christian Angels and Saints of Egyptian Nameless Gods. On the other, there is Curac which requires calling upon the name of the &quot;wild divinities&quot;, like the Celtic and Germanic pantheons. Finally, there is Veneficia, the magic which requires perfect balance between the man and the beast and calls upon the &quot;masked gods&quot; of the empires- like the Roman or the Incan gods, although they could also work with more modern principles. The other Blood Sorceries work by making a more.. specific contact with the gods, instead of just touching the divine through the dual aspects of the Man and the Beast. Ahranite Sorcery, for example, allows Shaddad to rest in the soul of each vampire who use its magic. Lithopedia makes contact with the spirits of the elements, while the Gilded Cage works with the spirits of the cities. Vodoun works by calling upon the Loa- mysterious spirits of the Underworld who resemble Geists in many ways. Merges Sorcery seeks after the blessings of Pazuzu and his demons. Other blood magics may also be found- and each allows the vampire to being his divine self into existence.<br /> <br /> Finally, few words about Father. After searching for eternity in the Abyss, he knew he couldn't make his dreams come true without the help of Lilith- yet she wasn't willing to help him. He was too mad, she told him. His touch would destroy vampires. Yet, he tried- creating a dark infestation which used the vampires as a gate to the Abyss. While that attempt is, more or less, a failure, another one was kinda successful. Mages, drawn by their hunger for knowledge and immortality, has made contact with a strong vampire who wished to see the Heavens, and using Minerva's support he helped them turning into the Breath Drinkers. Using that opportunity, he tricked the vampire who called himself Theban into sending his Breath Drinkers against a few powerful mages who were close to Archmastery- and after the fight revealed himself before them. Now, he had mages who were also vampires- eaters of souls who could unite the other Watchtowers into a single vision...<br /> <br /> Neither Lilith or Minerva has forgiven his betrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:28:54-07:00","id":465675,"title":"","content":"Interesting...<br /> <br /> What are your theories concerning Dracula and Longinus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:50:34-07:00","id":465685,"title":"","content":"Both of them are &quot;one time favors&quot; as one can call it- one was given by Lilith to Amoniel, an angel of the Empyrian (which may also be the entity behind the god Amon) and the other was by Lucifer (who noticed that the God Machine has targeted Dracula as a disturbance and wanted to &quot;help&quot;). As &quot;one time creations&quot; both of them are Clanless (some sort of super Revenants), and the chances are that they are still around- Dracula works in the shadows of the Order in order to free Lucifer from Inferno, while Longinus gathers the &quot;inere council&quot; of the Sanctified in Thebes, seeking to make God to return to the world (which is the mission given to him by Amoniel)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:17:47-07:00","id":467040,"title":"","content":"Very cool!<br /> <br /> Will you be doing a section on Hunters as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:52:16-07:00","id":467074,"title":"","content":"I am planing to- but I can't promise when.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T19:24:45-07:00","id":1206760,"title":"","content":"Lost,just one more question. The cosmology you posted in your blog yesterday. Does it agree with what you said in this thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T04:38:37-07:00","id":1206850,"title":"","content":"Well, it is mostly built upon the one presented in this thread- you may consider it as the first draft of the current cosmology. While I've changed few of the things, you could assume that unless there is a contradiction, it is still valid. In a case of contradiction, the new version gets prioritized. Of course, no one is going to force you to choose the new cosmology over the new one, so if you find some detail here as cool, you could use it in any way you like :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T15:01:16-07:00","id":1208201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/338498-mapping-the-stars-my-cosmology-thread?p=338511#post338511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That God-Machine was created by an ancient civilization was my initial personal interpretation, though change thousands to million years. Anyway, I like what I see here, and I'll follow the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> God always was. the GM is the alpha and Omega","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T15:40:10-07:00","id":1208221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/338498-mapping-the-stars-my-cosmology-thread?p=341072#post341072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaea is one of the two great spirits who rule Hisil- Ain Soph, who is the Breath of Life, and Gaea, the Mother of all Life. No one has ever saw Gaea, and many claim she does not exist. However, this is a nonsense- for every person who has set his foot in the Shadow has seen the Queen of Nature- for she is Hisil itself. After all, she is the spiritual reflection of the world itself- and so does the Shadow. One only needs to ask Occam what he would think about it, and there is the answer- Gaea is the Shadow of the world. While some claim that she had put the Gauntlet after loosing her beloved guardian, the truth is that the rise of the barrier was planned- once all the competitors were to spread their Essence as Hosts, the next level was to see which of the Hosts would survive the new world. Once, there were many more Hosts in the world- but one by one the were devoured by either the Uratha or the other players. Gaea is still waiting for a winner, although she is watching the Uratha in interest- for they are not officially players (or even tools) in the game, but they have so much power in the spirit world that she may eventually lose interest in the other spirits and recognize the Forsaken as her true guardians- something their Father won't like to see. The most interesting thing that has happened in the game was when one of the Progenitors, and idigam and the maker of the Bat Hosts, has decided to leave the game for a.. different game- the race for the Black Sun.<br /> <br /> The third problem in the myth is the idigams- those powerful beings were trapped on the Moon for years, returning only because of mankind's stupidity. This, however, was planned- not by Father Wolf, of course. He planned to get rid of them forever.<br /> <br /> It was Luna's plan.<br /> <br /> In many ways, Luna is almost like an idigam- the only thing which separates her from the Shapeless is her connection to the Moon. Luna's plan was to try and bind the mad creatures to herself as an alien army, to be used as a weapon for her own benefit and rising her Rank in the spirit world. While the idigams has proved themselves mercurial, Luna had all the time in the world. Eventually, they would tie themselves to her surface, becoming hers. Many has fallen to her through the generations- until one day, mankind first set foot on the Moon, giving the desperate idigams chance to escape their jailor. The one behind the events was no other than the Lemurian who slept in the dark side of the Moon- it wished to go back to Earth, and it grew attached to the wishes of the lonely beings who were its companions through the long years. And so, out of pure, selfish act, Death brought the idigams back with him to Earth. Still, Luna has managed to absorb a number of the weaker idigams into her, making them into her greatest servants.<br /> <br /> The last fact the the Uratha usually &amp;quot;forget&amp;quot; in their story is that there was not only a Father Wolf- there was also a Mother, Mother Wolf was the mother of the Firstborn, and she never quite liked her &amp;quot;mate's bastards&amp;quot;. She is still alive, and being one of the oldest spirits to ever walk the Shadow she is quite terrifying. She is the supporting power behind the Pure, and she sees the 5 Firstborn who support the Forsaken as traitors. While the 8 Firstborn are her and Father Wolf's best known children, there are other &amp;quot;Firstborn&amp;quot; out there, who hasn't chosen a Tribe or a side in the fight between the Pure and the Forsaken, between the Mother and the Father- Watcher Wolf, for example, or Talking Wolf. No one ever dares to mention her lost child before her- the one known as Soulless Wolf.<br /> <br /> Talking about Soulless Wolf, let us talk about the Maeljin. Those nine powerful spirits were the first spirits of Sin that were made by mankind. The Wounds are real wounds in the flesh of Gaea made by the flames of Inferno as they burn her. Gaea see the nine as her real threat, more than the idigams or any other mad spirits birthed by mankind. She needs to find someone who could help her destroy them without becoming them (as it happened so many times before). The Progenitors are still in the middle of their game, so no one is still ready to take the mantle of the leader. Maybe the Uratha could be a better choice for that mission- that is, if they'll stop killing each other.<br /> <br /> After the fall of Pangaea, the Uratha has created their first empire in Sumer. This is why Sumerian sounds so similar to First Tounge- this was the tongue of its leaders, and as such it has taken root in the early culture. Unihar, no longer being a child of two werewolves, is now the child of werewolf and a spirit. Every time a spirit tries to Claim a person, that person has a chance to devour the spirit instead, creating a &amp;quot;siten uzu&amp;quot; like claimed. About the Ancients- the Breath is the mirror of Ain Soph, in the same way the Nature (see in the future) is Gaea's twin- when the Gauntlet was risen, both those powerful spirits were split into a Flesh and Spirit aspects, and the Breath is Ain Soph's Flesh form. The Deep is one of the many old creations of the Lemurians, once worshiped by a small nation which was drowned with the fall of Lemuria, mutating him. The Flesh is the second woman of Adam, who shapes constantly out of rage of being rejected. The Mother was one of Luna's handmaidens who objected her relationships with Father Wolf, and as such it was teared down by the great hunter and became an Host (a thing which gave Gaea the idea for creating the contest), and now she became complete again. The Unseen was the first fear of mankind who took form. Zmai the Worm is the origin of the Nosferatu clan and a member in the Coalition of Blood.<br /> <br /> About shapeshifters- the Colony was made by one of the Nameless Gods, one known as Bast. The Distant ones and the Brineborn are created by Gaea's twin children- Sea and Sky, and each made their children as gifts to their mother. The Unclean are a late creation, born from a great city spirit who made them in order to connect all the world and eventually become the spirit of mankind. The Baal Hadad are, of course, Helios's soldiers in his game against his sister Luna- although some has been fallen to corruption under the influence of the once great, now fallen servant of the Sun- Moloch. The Faceless are a strange breed of shifters who can take the forms of other people- made by no other than the Flesh itself. The bat people from WatP are an &amp;quot;evolved&amp;quot; form of the Bat Host of the Obsidian Butterfly. The Chacma are the creations of the ghosts of old tribes of mankind. The wereheynas are Helios's first (and failed) children. The werejackals are a lost group of Uratha, long corrupted by the forces of Duat and Anpu into their current form as the guardians of the dead.<br /> <br /> And that's for the shadow- next time, we go to the underworld!</div> </div> </div> </div>now that we know of the Border Marches and that Father Wolf was an Pangaean instead of a spirit,does it change anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:23:03-07:00","id":1208574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/338498-mapping-the-stars-my-cosmology-thread?p=1208221#post1208221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> now that we know of the Border Marches and that Father Wolf was an Pangaean instead of a spirit,does it change anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, things have been changed in my cosmological view with or without the reveal in Sundered world. While I'll detail it more in upcoming interviews and cosmology posts, a taste for my vision for Father Wolf's origin could be seen in what I wrote in Chris Allen's excellent post for<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171004-ten-spirits-binded?p=1173037#post1173037\"> Ten Spirits Binded</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\